<p class="sheets-lead">Spreadsheets in a page, computed on the server:
<code>{pad:open/}sheet:grid{pad:close/}</code> takes its cells as lines of text, a comma between them, or
the rows of <code>data=</code>, and writes a table of what the formulas come to - =B2*C2,
=SUM(D2:D9), =VLOOKUP(E2,$I$2:$J$6,2) - with the column letters and the row numbers around it.
The formulas are spreadsheet syntax, read by a parser of their own, and call the
{$functions} functions of <code>pad/subs/formulas/types/</code>, which answer what Excel
answers. <code>editable</code> makes cells fields that post back and are computed again - in a
form, or in a live region without a script of the page's own.</p>

<ul class="sheets-cards">
  {array:sheets}
    <li><a class="sheets-card" href="?{$page}"><b>{$name}</b><span>{$line}</span></a></li>
  {/array:sheets}
  <li><a class="sheets-card" href="?functions"><b>Functions</b><span>Every function a formula can call, what it does and an example of it on a sample sheet.</span></a></li>
</ul>

